(KEY-25 — `fork` is an expression, not a statement: it returns 0 in the
 child and the child's PID in the parent, and the trailing `the process` is
 optional (bare `fork` also works). The parent reaps before printing so the
 two processes' output cannot interleave.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox KEY-25.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   child ran
   parent saw a positive pid
   bare fork also returned a pid
)
Set pid to fork the process.
If pid is 0 then,
    Print "child ran",
    Exit 0.
Set reaped to reap child pid.
If pid is greater than 0 then,
    Print "parent saw a positive pid".
Set 'the second pid' to fork.
If 'the second pid' is 0 then,
    Exit 0.
Set 'the second reaped' to reap child 'the second pid'.
If 'the second pid' is greater than 0 then,
    Print "bare fork also returned a pid".
